  "description": "PUKNUI crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C114 H210 Eu16 F18 N4 O48,2(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu9 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu1 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu10 (Eu) has 3 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 3 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu8 (Eu) has 3 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu11 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu12 (Eu) has 3 O neighbors; Eu13 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu14 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu15 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu16 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu17 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu1A? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors; Eu7? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 30 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.485-3.858 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.38-101.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu16(μ4-F)6(μ3-F)12(tBuCOO)18[N(CH2CH2O)3]4·2EtOH.",
